25,2,1,talk,Midori,,It seems we have a habit of losing ownership during crises and failing to adapt our scope to business changes.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Our physical reality is harsh. Peak season is a blackout for changes, and our hardware is outdated.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,May,,We have a history of skipping upgrades and dealing with messy data migrations from external teams.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We are losing key internal knowledge, and the depot staff often ignore standardized training.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Interestingly, the board prefers operating expenses over capital, and bundled pricing has been more stable than modular ones.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, if the hardware is that bad, we need a vendor who can actually survive the yard.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,Exactly. A generic cloud tool might just be another thing we wrap in spreadsheets.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, if the staff ignores trainers, a partner-led rollout might be a waste of money.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Misaki,,I agree. We need someone who stays on-site or understands the actual human friction.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,And we must avoid a modular licensing nightmare that creeps up on us every year.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, so a fixed-price or bundled approach is safer for the budget?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,pass,Ryuji,,Skip,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
37,2,3,pass,May,,Skip,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
38,2,3,pass,Misaki,,Skip,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. The ""hidden"" costs of separate licenses are where the real danger lies.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Midori,,"We need a balance of stability, on-site presence, and a predictable cost structure.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
